      "caveat": "P-0024249 — Mutations: 3 of 7 rows (rows Annotation (OncoKB) contains “Oncogenic”); Copy Number Alterations: 3 rows; Structural Variants: 3 rows. Each table lists a variant, a gene's call or an event once however many of the patient's samples carry it (Samples names them); allele frequency and read counts are the highest among those samples. Copy number is the deep calls only (AMP, HOMDEL), as the portal's patient view lists them; Copy # on a mutation is the gene's deep calls anywhere in the patient. Cohort % is the share of the study's samples profiled for the gene by their panel with a mutation in it, or with the same copy-number call. Annotation is OncoKB v7.5 (oncogenicity and its highest sensitivity level); structural variants carry the study's own annotation, not OncoKB's. The patient list: 3,211 patients. Sorted by Structural Variants (highest first), missing values last, across the cohort; every page is a slice of that one order, and the download holds every row kept, with every column. ",
